# Testing & build

## Python (pytest)

```powershell
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest              # default: -m 'not integration'
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest -m integration  # real-browser CDP tests
```

- Config: `pyproject.toml` (`testpaths = ["tests"]`, `timeout = 60`)
- Integration marker for Chrome/Edge CDP flows

## JavaScript (Vitest)

```powershell
npm test
npm run test:perf              # table render/query + boot curtain perf budgets
npm run lint                    # ESLint weight guardrails (warnings)
npm run check:module-size       # js/*.js line cap (3800)
npm run check:bundle-size       # requires npm run build first
npm run perf:profile            # regenerate tests/fixtures/perf-profile/
npm run perf:audit              # Playwright timing (server must be running)
```

- Config: `vitest.config.js`
- Tests in `tests/*.test.js` and `tests/js/*.test.js`

## Full suite

```powershell
.\scripts\test-all.ps1           # ruff + pytest + vitest
.\scripts\test-all.ps1 -Full     # + module-size, lint, build, bundle-size, dist-integrity, audit_free_surface_data
```

**Line budgets** (`pytest tests/test_repo_size_budgets.py`): `server.py` **3000**; `scripts/git_tree.py` **720**. Module-size: `js/*.js` **3800** (`table-query.worker.js` exempt).

## Frontend build (optional)

```powershell
npm run build   # esbuild → dist/; serve with BAKLOG_SERVE_BUILT=1 (frozen exe auto-serves when dist/ is bundled)
```

- Source: `scripts/build-frontend.mjs`
- Tailwind: committed `tailwind.css` (precompiled from `styles/tailwind-input.css`)

